      "id": "clai_00004",
      "type": "claim",
      "surface_form": "When applied to a set of 1,585 crystals with elastic properties, CGCNN predicts bulk modulus with a mean absolute error of 0.077 log(GPa) and shear modulus with a mean absolute error of 0.114 log(GPa), demonstrating good generalization."
    },
    {
      "id": "clai_00078",
      "type": "claim",
      "surface_form": "Continuous-filter convolutional (cfconv) layers enable convolution on arbitrarily positioned inputs, overcoming the limitations of discrete filters that require grid-aligned data."
    },
    {
      "id": "clai_00130",
      "type": "claim",
      "surface_form": "The Message Passing Neural Network (MPNN) achieves state‑of‑the‑art performance on all QM9 regression targets, reaching chemical accuracy on 11 of the 13 targets and outperforming prior models such as SchNet and DTNN."
    },
    {
      "id": "clai_00133",
      "type": "claim",
      "surface_form": "A general training method allows MPNNs to use larger node representation dimensions without increasing computation time or memory, providing substantial savings over previous high‑dimensional MPNNs."
    },
    {
      "id": "clai_00137",
      "type": "claim",
      "surface_form": "The Message Passing Neural Network framework unifies eight previously proposed graph‑based neural models under a single formalism."
    },
    {
      "id": "clai_00138",
      "type": "claim",
      "surface_form": "Learning directly from molecular graphs without handcrafted descriptors enables the MPNN to achieve lower prediction errors than descriptor‑based methods."
    },
    {
      "id": "clai_00139",
      "type": "claim",
      "surface_form": "Across all QM9 properties, the MPNN reduces the mean absolute error by 30–70 % relative to the best previously reported graph‑neural‑network baseline."
    },
    {
      "id": "clai_00140",
      "type": "claim",
      "surface_form": "For internal energy at 0 K (U0), enthalpy (H), Gibbs free energy (G), heat capacity at constant volume (Cv), and highest vibrational frequency (Ω), the MPNN records lower mean absolute errors than SchNet and DTNN (U0 MAE 0.45 vs 0.55/0.72; H 0.39 vs 0.59/0.80; G 0.44 vs 0.55/0.74; Cv 0.80 vs 0.99/1.71; Ω 0.19 vs 0.41/0.78)."
    },
    {
      "id": "clai_00317",
      "type": "claim",
      "surface_form": "Graph network models (CGCNN and MEGNet) have high errors on small datasets (<10^4 samples) but leverage large datasets more efficiently, outperforming traditional ML and AutoML approaches on tasks with approximately 10^4 data points or more."
    },
    {
      "id": "clai_00321",
      "type": "claim",
      "surface_form": "Graph networks (CGCNN and MEGNet) far outperform traditional ML algorithms on formation energy prediction tasks, with MEGNet decisively outperforming Automatminer for the PhDOS task; among nine structure-based tasks, Automatminer and MEGNet each achieve best scores on 4 tasks."
    },
    {
      "id": "clai_00492",
      "type": "claim",
      "surface_form": "Elemental embedding vectors learned by the crystal formation‑energy MEGNet model reproduce known periodic‑table trends and, when transferred to band‑gap and elastic‑moduli models, reduce their mean absolute errors, improving upon prior machine‑learning approaches."
